<title>UK: Shell sees Brent throughput rising in October.</title>
<headline>Shell sees Brent throughput rising in October.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-09-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brent system operator Shell Exploration and Production (Shell Expro) on Friday estimated North Sea Brent crude system throughput in October at 499,985 barrels per day (bpd), up from 477,148 bpd in September.</p>
<p>Average Brent pipeline throughput for the year to the end of August was 487,471 bpd, Shell said.</p>
<p>Brent system throughput includes crude produced from 13 fields and several satellite wells piped to the Sullom Voe terminal in the Shetland Islands for blending with Ninian crude and exported as Brent Blend.</p>
<p>Shell Expro, a joint venture between Royal Dutch/Shell Group and Exxon Corp, said the throughput forecast was preliminary and may be &quot;subject to significant fluctuation.&quot;</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7930</p>
</text>
